up|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West definitely had an aggressive overbid, and as you can see, even 3@H goes down. You need at least a good 10 or 11 to jump to 4@H. Further, this illustrates why you preempt. You take up bidding room for the opponents and they have less room to bid, meaning they often have to guess what to do.|
PG| ***** 36 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would probably pass 2@S with the West hand although double is not terrible. Then I think North should pass and East should pass. In 2@S we end up taking five spade tricks, one heart, and two diamonds for 8 tricks which makes the double even more aggressive.|
PG| ***** 37 ***** |


